course: dictionary
lesson: 70
title: Acoustic: sound and hearing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Acoustic means to do with sound or hearing. An acoustic instrument makes its sound without electric power, so an acoustic guitar is one you play without plugging it in.
explain: «An electric guitar has a solid body and is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier; an acoustic guitar has a hollow body that makes it louder without electricity.» The clues are plugged into an amplifier and without electricity, so acoustic means it needs no electric power.
explain: Acoustics, in the plural, means how well sound carries in a room or hall. Try your meaning in the sentence: acoustic music is music played on instruments that use no electric power. That makes sense, so you have it.
fact: Acoustic means to do with sound or hearing.
fact: An acoustic instrument, such as a guitar or piano, makes sound without electric power.
fact: Acoustic music is played on acoustic instruments, not electric ones.
fact: «Acoustics» (plural) means how well sound carries in a room or hall.
fact: Informally, «an acoustic» means an acoustic guitar.
exercise: «An electric guitar is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier.» What does acoustic mean in «an acoustic guitar»? | Painted in bright colours | Makes sound only when plugged in | *Makes sound without electric power
exercise: «The concert hall had good acoustics, so every singer could be heard clearly.» What are acoustics? | The seats in the front rows | *How well sound carries in a room or hall | A kind of musical note
exercise: Acoustic music is played on instruments without electric power. Which of these would make acoustic music? | A radio that runs on batteries | *A wooden piano | An electric keyboard plugged into the wall
test: Acoustic means to do with what? | *Sound or hearing | Speed and movement | Colour or light
test: Which of these describes acoustics? | How fast a car can go | How heavy a school bag is | *How well sound carries in a room
exam: Maya says an acoustic guitar must be plugged into a wall to work. Is she right? | Yes, but only when it is raining | Yes, it always needs a plug to make any sound | *No, it makes its sound without electric power
